  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Water supply and Sanitation Development in Small Towns and Rural Growth Centres under the EU-MDG -Initiative</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p&gt;To improve access to Water and Sanitation aiming at halving the proportion of the population without sustainable access to safe drinking water and basic sanitation ,as stated under the Millennium Development Goal 7c(MDG 7c). The total EU contribution, under the EU Millennium Development Goals initiative is 30,500,000 Euros , and it will be used to do the following: -1. Access to safe piped water supply for at least 350,000 people (and for a design population of 630,000, considering a 20 years population projection) in line with national standards in terms of service quality, quantity and distance as well as water quality and source protection; -2. Adequate sanitation for the same target population, by achieving 100% latrine coverage promoting the improvement of sanitation facilities through an incentive scheme, and improving the environmental health situation by constructing public toilets and sludge treatment facilities; &lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
